    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That emptiness is the hardest kind of silence to sit with, and it's okay to let it be exactly what it is for now. The graveyard you see isn't a failure—it's the compost for whatever wants to grow next, even if that takes months or years. You don't have to force a single color onto the canvas today; just let the silence be a room you exist in, not a verdict on your worth. Your story isn't over because you've paused—it's just that the next chapter hasn't learned to speak yet.",
